const e="panjab-university-zonal-youth-festival",h=2026,t="Source: the Panjab University Youth & Heritage Festivals Information and Rules Booklet, September 2026 (65 pages), linked as the current Youth & Heritage Festivals Rules on the Department of Youth Welfare website. The template cites the August 2016 booklet (the 2021 and 2024 booklets also exist); the 2026 edition is the newest and is used here. Differences from 2016 that matter: Light Vocal time 6 minutes (was 5); Classical Dance 8 to 10 minutes with live accompaniment only; Hand Writing Competition added (item 26, not carried by the template); stage-setting 10 minutes for One Act Play, Indian Orchestra and Folk Orchestra; the second and third place can be recommended to the Inter-Zonal Festival; entry fee Rs. 11 per student (was Rs. 5); a 2016 rule on a spare artist is replaced by 'do not write the name of a spare student'. The booklet prints no zonal or inter-zonal dates or venues (the Department notifies them), no news, and no marks or points for judging (only first, second and third; overall trophy scores are printed). The Heritage Festival rules (pages 45 to 55) are in Punjabi in a legacy font; the template does not carry heritage items, so they are named in one line per class under page key other and their rules are not captured. The booklet gives no registration deadline. The template has one age group (Open (College)), so every eligibility point is event-wide. The Light Vocal, Shabad/Bhajan, Instrumental and Creative Writing template items each cover booklet items that the booklet lists separately.",a=JSON.parse(`{"Title":"Rules & Criteria","Subtitle":"Panjab University Youth Festival (Zonal and Inter-Zonal). Read these rules before you register.","NoticeTitle":"Please Read Before Registering","Notice":"Only students of Panjab University colleges, regional centres and teaching departments may take part, and each student must be under 25 on 1 July of the session. Dates and venues are announced by the Department of Youth Welfare.","Notes":["Zonal festival dates: {{ZonalFestivalDates}}. Zonal venue: {{ZonalFestivalVenue}}.","Inter-Zonal festival dates: {{InterZonalFestivalDates}}. Inter-Zonal venue: {{InterZonalFestivalVenue}}.","Questions: {{DepartmentContact}}."],"Sections":[{"Key":"general","Title":"General Rules","Items":["The Youth Festival is organised by the Department of Youth Welfare, Panjab University, at three levels: Zonal, Inter-Zonal, and Inter-University, National and International.","There are 35 Youth Festival items in five groups: Music (9 items), Dance (4), Theatre (5), Literary (8) and Fine Arts (9).","A Heritage Festival is held with the Youth Festival. It has its own items (see Other Information).","Up to 5 minutes are given for exit, stage-setting and entry for every stage item. One Act Play, Indian Orchestra and Folk Orchestra get up to 10 minutes.","In special cases the judges may give up to 5 more minutes for stage-setting.","Aims of the festivals: to channel the energy of young students into creative and useful fields; to give an atmosphere of creativity and group work; to build patriotism and nationalism and acquaint students with their cultural heritage; to give chances for self-development, character building, leadership, mutual tolerance and fellow feeling; to acquaint students with heritage, cultural values, rituals, folklore and way of life; and to preserve and promote heritage, folklore and traditional culture through art and craft."]},{"Key":"eligibility","Title":"Eligibility","Items":["Entry is open to all bona fide students of affiliated colleges, constituent colleges, regional centres and University Teaching Departments.","{{AgeLimit}}.","At the Zonal Festival, a student may take part at most three times at undergraduate level and two times at postgraduate level.","A student who joined a professional course after graduation or post-graduation may take part for the normal length of that academic programme.","A student may take part in at most five items of the same Youth Festival.","Heritage Festival entries are counted separately: a student who took part in any number of Youth Festival items may also take part in up to three Heritage Festival items in the same session.","If two items that a student has entered are held at the same time, the student must settle it at the home college when the host college cannot change the schedule.","Combined teams (students from more than one institution) are not allowed up to the Inter-Zonal Festival.","Team members are not replaced in normal circumstances. In special cases a member of a group item may be replaced for the Inter-Zonal Festival with prior approval of the Director Youth Welfare. The substitute is counted as having used one chance in that item at the Zonal Festival of that session.","An evening shift is treated like a separate college, so its students may take part independently.","Only students who actually perform are named on the entry form, within the maximum number of participants of the item. Do not write the name of an extra or spare student.","The student's name, father's name, date of birth, age on 1 July, class, roll number, registration number, year of passing +2, items, how many times the student took part earlier in Zonal Youth Festivals, address and phone number are written on the student entry form.","The Principal verifies the entry form and attests the photograph."]},{"Key":"registration","Title":"How to Register","Items":["The college sends entry forms to the convener of its zone. The forms must be complete in every way.","Fill in the forms in block letters or type them, to avoid spelling mistakes in certificates.","Form I is the entry form of the college: zone, session, venue, dates, college, contingent in-charge with contact number or email, total number of student participants (male and female), total number of teachers and directors, total number of professional accompanists, and the items. The Principal signs it with the office seal.","Send a separate form for each student (Form II), each teacher (Form III), each accompanist (Form IV) and each item (Form V) with Form I.","Form V lists the actual performers of the item with father's name, date of birth, class and roll number, gender and the earlier chances used at the Zonal Festival (undergraduate and postgraduate level), and the accompanists (student or professional, and nature of duty). The contingent in-charge and the Principal sign it.","Write the names of student accompanists in the accompanists column.","An incomplete entry form is not accepted in any case.","Entries must follow the rules in the Information and Rules booklet strictly.","Photocopies of the entry forms printed in the booklet may be used.","The organising secretary of each Zonal Festival checks the entry forms and makes sure all details are correct.","Entry forms of all items recommended for the Inter-Zonal Festival are sent by the zone convener to the Principal or Convener of the Inter-Zonal Festival, with a copy to the Department of Youth Welfare, immediately after the Zonal Festival.","Each student at the Inter-Zonal Festival must carry an identity card with a photograph and show it when asked. Boarding, lodging and entry to the auditorium are allowed only with the identity card and badge. The Department sends specimens of the card to zone conveners or heads of institutions.","The Department does not issue identity cards for Zonal Festivals. The convener of a Zonal Festival may arrange them.","Participants must report to the stage secretary at least 15 minutes before the item starts. Late-comers are likely to lose their chance."]},{"Key":"fees","Title":"Fees and Contributions","Items":["Zonal Youth Festival entry fee: {{ZonalYouthEntryFee}}. The head of the institution pays it directly to the convener of the Zonal Youth Festival.","The fee is charged on the number of students on the college rolls, whatever the number of items sent, and even if the institution sends no item.","Zonal Heritage Festival entry fee: {{ZonalHeritageEntryFee}}, charged in the same way.","At the Zonal Festival each college also pays a contribution to the host college: {{HostContribution}}. It may be paid from the amalgamated fund or any other fund of the college, whether or not the college takes part. The Principal of the host college gives the utilisation certificate to the contributing colleges within 30 days.","At the Inter-Zonal level there is no entry fee and no contribution fee.","The University gives a subsidy for each festival from the Youth Welfare Fund Account: {{UniversitySubsidy}}.","For the Inter-Zonal Festival, the Principal or Convener sends the estimated expenditure through the Director Youth Welfare, and 75 percent of the subsidy is released after the Vice-Chancellor approves it.","Objection fee: {{ObjectionFee}} (see Complaints)."]},{"Key":"dates","Title":"Dates","Items":["Zonal Youth and Heritage Festival dates: {{ZonalFestivalDates}}.","Inter-Zonal Youth and Heritage Festival dates: {{InterZonalFestivalDates}}, notified well in time.","Inter-University, National and International festivals are held when they are allotted to Panjab University."]},{"Key":"venue","Title":"Venue and Hosting","Items":["Zonal Festival venue: {{ZonalFestivalVenue}}. Any institution of the zone may host the festival of its zone.","When more than one institution of a zone offers to host, the zone co-ordinator or the Director Youth Welfare decides the venue by lots.","Inter-Zonal Festival venue: {{InterZonalFestivalVenue}}. Any affiliated institution may choose to host it. The Department of Youth Welfare decides the dates and venue.","Heritage Festivals are held with the Zonal Youth Festivals. If a zone's Youth Festival is not held, the Department decides how to hold that zone's Heritage Festival.","The head of the host institution of the last Zonal Festival is the ex-officio Co-ordinator of the Zone. The Co-ordinator holds meetings of the heads of institutions of the zone to propose dates, venue and other arrangements, as the Department instructs.","The head of the host institution is the convener of the festival. The convener appoints an organising secretary from the teaching staff, may appoint a camp commandant from the lecturers to look after food and stay, and appoints committees of teaching staff.","Student volunteers of the host institution may help the committees. Teaching staff other than the organising secretary and camp commandant must also help with compering.","At the Inter-Zonal Festival the Department may name trained teachers, employees or students of other institutions as volunteers, if the convener asks.","Each contingent must stay in the accommodation the organisers give. Only participants, actual accompanists, teacher or student directors, contingent in-charges, volunteers and organisers may stay in the festival accommodation.","Incoming participants tell the convener or organising secretary how they will travel and when they will arrive.","Free meals are given only during the Inter-Zonal Festival, only to student participants, teacher or student directors, contingent in-charges, accompanists and volunteers named by the Department. Student volunteers of the host college and organising committee members who must be present day and night also get free meals. The mess opens half a day before the festival and closes half a day after it.","At a Zonal Festival the convener decides the meal arrangements and charges, with the standing committee."]},{"Key":"levels","Title":"Levels and Qualification","Items":["Youth Festivals go from the Zonal Festival to the Inter-Zonal Festival. Teams and individuals picked from the Inter-Zonal Festival are recommended for Inter-University, National and International Youth Festivals and similar programmes.","Combined teams may be sent to those festivals to get better results. The Director Youth Welfare decides.","The Director may hold preparatory meetings, workshops and talks with experts to prepare teams for Inter-University festivals.","At the Zonal Festival, the individual or team in first and second place is recommended for the Inter-Zonal Festival. If they cannot take part for any reason, the third place may be recommended, and so on.","The number of entries a zone sends to the Inter-Zonal Festival is given for each item.","Judges may decide not to consider an entry for a position when the performance is below standard. That entry is then stopped from taking part in the next higher festival. This applies to both Zonal and Inter-Zonal festivals.","A contingent coming to a Zonal Festival is led by a contingent in-charge named by the head of the institution.","A zone's whole contingent for the Inter-Zonal Festival is led by one teacher as contingent in-charge named by the convener of the Zonal Festival. If the convener fails to name one, the Director Youth Welfare names a lecturer of the zone.","For the Inter-University and National or International festivals, the Director may name two in-charges, one male and one female.","The convener of a zone may refuse to send the entry form to the Inter-Zonal Festival of participants who did not behave well at the Zonal Festival."]},{"Key":"teams","Title":"Entries from an Institution or Zone","Items":["At the Zonal Festival each institution sends the number of participants or teams shown for each item.","At the Inter-Zonal Festival each zone sends the winners of its Zonal Festival, in the number shown for each item (first and second position for most items).","An entry may not have more participants than the maximum printed for the item."]},{"Key":"conduct","Title":"Conduct and Discipline","Items":["All teachers, students, accompanists, volunteers and organisers must help to keep perfect discipline.","Only teacher in-charges and students set the stage and sound within the time given. No outsider may go on stage for this. The organising secretary checks the identity cards: the registration card, Pupin card or identity card given by the Principal.","After the item, the stage manager of the host college introduces only the student artists and teachers. Students may not speak or perform during the introduction.","Disturbance, rowdyism, indiscipline, drinking, vulgar or obscene songs, eve teasing, influencing the judges, indecent behaviour, undignified acts and being absent from rooms between 11 p.m. and 6 a.m. are against the spirit of the festival. They may lead to withdrawal of all privileges and amenities, and to disqualification from future festivals.","Participants, directors, contingent in-charges and accompanists must keep their badges and identity cards with them and stay at the places given to them. They must keep the festival premises and their rooms clean.","Contingent in-charges and teacher directors must make sure that nobody other than the eligible persons stays with the participants.","Nobody may leave the campus before the festival is over without the convener's permission.","Everyone must go back to their rooms right after the stage programme, camp-fire or late rehearsal.","Meals are served only in the campus dining hall at the stated times. Late-comers are not served.","Organisers do not take responsibility for heavy cash and valuables. Teams and individuals must make their own arrangements with lock and key.","Heads of institutions must make sure that participants are medically fit and vaccinated against contagious and infectious diseases before they are sent.","All individuals and incoming teams, including teachers and accompanists, must follow the campus rules.","The convener of a Zonal or Inter-Zonal festival may take any suitable action for a breach of campus rules, misconduct or indiscipline by any member of a contingent or the member's associates.","No participating institution may go to the media directly about any aspect of the organisation of a Panjab University youth festival.","A contingent of girl participants only, with no lady teacher otherwise accompanying it, may bring a lady escort. This applies to both Zonal and Inter-Zonal Youth Festivals.","Organisers should give incentives to the most popular, social and disciplined teams or individuals, so that participants keep a good atmosphere."]},{"Key":"judging","Title":"Judging and Results","Items":["Performances are judged only as first, second and third. No marks are published.","No bracketed prizes are given in first and second positions.","Prizes and certificates go to the student who actually performed.","The decision of the judges is final in every case. In a complaint of a very serious nature, the Vice-Chancellor may over-rule a decision.","Results are preferably announced at the end of each session of a festival.","After the result, only the Principal or teacher in charge of the team may take tips from the judges for better performance in future."]},{"Key":"complaints","Title":"Complaints and Objections","Items":["Complaints or objections about the judges' decision are not accepted at any level.","Complaints may be made against teams or participants for breaking university rules.","General objections or complaints about a Zonal Youth Festival are considered by the standing committee of the zone.","An objection or complaint about an item is accepted only within 30 minutes after that item ends.","The contingent in-charge, with the consent of the Principal of the college, makes the objection with documented proof.","The objection is addressed to the convener of the standing committee (the Principal of the host college), with the full address and contact details of the complaining teacher and the objection fee of {{ObjectionFee}}.","The fee is refunded if the objection is upheld. If it is ruled out, the fee goes to the youth festival fund of the host college.","The standing committee looks into the matter on the papers given with the complaint. The decision is given before the next level festival is held.","If the objection is upheld, the standing committee decides the punishment. It may be disqualification in the current festival, or disqualification of that college from that item in future festivals and programmes of the University.","If the objection is ruled out, it may be treated as a waste of time or an attempt to defame the team or college. The committee may act against the complaining college.","Rowdyism or indiscipline may lead to cancelling the participation of the team or students. The standing committee may also disqualify the item or the students from future Panjab University festivals and programmes."]},{"Key":"points","Title":"Overall Trophies and Scores","Items":["These overall trophies are given for the overall performance of the institutions, with runner-up and second runner-up trophies: the Panjab University Zonal Trophy (Zonal level) and the Panjab University Vice-Chancellor's Trophy (Inter-Zonal level).","For a co-education institution that enters both Gidha and Bhangra at a Zonal or Inter-Zonal festival, only the better score of the two counts in the overall score sheet kept by the host institution.","If any team, participant or accompanist is declared disqualified or debarred for indiscipline or breaking rules, that college is not eligible for the overall trophy."]},{"Key":"prizes","Title":"Prizes and Awards","Items":["Prizes are given only as books, mementoes or trophies.","Some individuals with outstanding performance in a group item may be judged Commended. The best of them is Commended First, the next Commended Second, and so on.","In addition to the Commended awards, suitable prizes may be given to members of winning teams in group items at a Zonal and Inter-Zonal Youth Festival, with the approval of the standing committee.","A student accompanist gets a certificate. Student accompanists may get participation or winner certificates at both Zonal and Inter-Zonal Youth Festivals.","At the Inter-Zonal Youth Festival, a solo winner (first position), members of a winning group team (first position) and those Commended First in group items get a university insignia with a university merit certificate.","At the Zonal and Inter-Zonal Youth and Heritage Festivals, solo participants in the first three positions, members of group teams in the first three positions and those Commended First, Second and Third in group items get a certificate of merit.","At the Zonal Youth and Heritage Festivals, a solo winner (first position) and members of a winning group team (first position) get college colours from their own institution.","All other participants of the Zonal and Inter-Zonal Youth and Heritage Festivals get a certificate of participation.","Panjab University Roll of Honour: for a student who represents India or Panjab University in an officially sponsored international event, or gets distinction in the All India Inter University Youth Festival (AIU) or the National Youth Festival (Government of India), and also took part in the Panjab University Inter-Zonal Festival.","Panjab University Colour: for a student who takes part in the All India Inter University Youth Festival (AIU) or the National Youth Festival, or gets distinction in the North Zone Inter University Youth Festival (AIU) or the Punjab State Inter Youth Festival (organised by a government organisation), and also took part in the Panjab University Inter-Zonal Festival.","For these two awards, the student must have the recommendation of the Department of Youth Welfare, must not be in any anti-social or indisciplinary activity, and must have no inquiry pending. The student applies through the college Principal on Form No. VI.","Distinction in Youth Leadership Training, Hiking and Trekking, Rock Climbing Camps, Cycle Tours, Mountaineering Course, Adventure Course and Allied Sports of Panjab University counts as equal to the Panjab University Inter-Zonal Youth or Heritage Festival.","The Director Youth Welfare may hold a special programme to honour distinguished students, teachers and heads of institutions who brought honour to the University in these festivals. Heads of institutions may honour teachers who help with the festivals."]},{"Key":"reporting","Title":"Accounts and Records","Items":["For the Zonal Festival, the Principal or Convener sends the utilisation certificate and the expenditure and income statement, attested by a Chartered Accountant, within 30 days from the close of the festival. Then the full subsidy is released.","For the Inter-Zonal Festival, the rest 25 percent of the subsidy is released after the same certificate and statement.","The Principal or Convener keeps all records, including result sheets, original bills, vouchers, quotations and receipts, for at least three years.","Any saving is sent by the Principal or Convener of the host college to the Director Youth Welfare, to be put in the Youth Welfare Fund Account."]},{"Key":"payments","Title":"Payments and Expenses","Items":["T.A. and D.A. of participants, accompanists, teachers, directors and contingent in-charges are paid by their own institutions.","Judges and the Quiz Master are paid as follows: {{JudgesPayment}}","Judges, experts and guests invited to the festivals may travel by their own car, taxi or AC chair car, whatever their grade pay or salary."]},{"Key":"other","Title":"Other Information","Items":["Hand Writing Competition (Punjabi, Hindi, Sanskrit and English) is item 26 of the Youth Festival. This template does not carry it.","Heritage Festival, Folk Music items (vocal and instrumental): Ladies Traditional and Ritualistic Songs of Punjab, Kavishri, Vaar Singing, Kali Singing and Folk Instruments.","Heritage Festival, Folk Dance items: Jhumar, Malwai Gidha, Sammi and Luddi.","Heritage Festival, Heritage Literary items: Heritage Quiz and Muhavredar Vaartalap.","Heritage Festival, Folk Theatre item: Bhand.","Heritage Festival, Art and Craft items: Guddian Patole Making, Chhikku Making, Pranda Making, Naala Making, Tokri Making, Mitti De Khidaune, Khiddo Making, Peerhi Making, Rassa Vattna, Eennu Making, Embroidery (Phulkari, Bagh, Dasuti or Cross Stitch), Pakhi Designing, Crochet Work, Knitting and Mehndi Designing.","In the Art and Fine Arts items at the Zonal and Inter-Zonal Festivals, the works are displayed right after the results are announced.","The host college may arrange a non-competitive Folk Art and Craft Exhibition during the festival, to show traditional artefacts and rare folk art to young students.","For students at Inter-University Youth Festivals, attendance is given for a maximum of ten days of rehearsals, plus the festival days and the journey. During the festival days the internal papers are adjusted on the recommendation of the Director Youth Welfare, if needed."]}],"Documents":[{"Title":"Panjab University Youth & Heritage Festivals - Information and Rules Booklet (September 2026)","Url":"https://youthwelfare.puchd.ac.in/pu-yw-information-and-rules-booklet-2026.pdf"}]}`),n=[{ParticipantType:"Individual",Source:"Booklet 2026 p.13 rule 4, p.15 rule 12, p.20 rule 20",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:["A grace of 15 seconds is allowed in every individual item."],Rules:["A teacher or student director is allowed in the individual items of music and dance."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:["In the other individual items (debate, poem recitation, elocution, creative writing, fine arts, histrionics and mimicry), a participant who is accompanied by a teacher or student director loses the right to take part."],Judging:null,Points:["Overall trophy score for an individual item: first place 5 points, second place 3 points, third place 1 point."],Notes:null},Markdown:`## Time and format
- A grace of 15 seconds is allowed in every individual item.

## Rules
- A teacher or student director is allowed in the individual items of music and dance.

## Not allowed
- In the other individual items (debate, poem recitation, elocution, creative writing, fine arts, histrionics and mimicry), a participant who is accompanied by a teacher or student director loses the right to take part.

## Points
- Overall trophy score for an individual item: first place 5 points, second place 3 points, third place 1 point.`},{ParticipantType:"Team",Source:"Booklet 2026 p.13 rule 4, p.15 rule 12, p.20 rule 20",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:["A grace of 30 seconds is allowed in every group item."],Rules:["A teacher or student director is allowed in every group item."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:["Overall trophy score for a group item with six or more participants on stage: first place 10 points, second place 7 points, third place 5 points.","Overall trophy score for a group item with two to five participants on stage: first place 7 points, second place 5 points, third place 3 points."],Notes:null},Markdown:`## Time and format
- A grace of 30 seconds is allowed in every group item.

## Rules
- A teacher or student director is allowed in every group item.

## Points
- Overall trophy score for a group item with six or more participants on stage: first place 10 points, second place 7 points, third place 5 points.
- Overall trophy score for a group item with two to five participants on stage: first place 7 points, second place 5 points, third place 3 points.`}],o=[],i=JSON.parse(`[{"Title":"Light Vocal (Geet/Ghazal/Folk Song)","Source":"Booklet 2026 p.23 Light Vocal, p.2 table","Sections":{"About":["Light Vocal has two categories: Ghazal and Geet, and Folk Song."],"TimeAndFormat":["Each participant gets up to 6 minutes. Maximum 1 participant and 3 accompanists for each category."],"Rules":["At the Zonal Festival each institution sends two participants: one from the Ghazal or Geet category and one from the Folk Song category.","At the Inter-Zonal Festival each zone sends one participant from Ghazal (first position), one from Geet (first position) and two from Folk Song (first and second position).","A student may not take part in more than one category.","Harmonium is allowed.","Up to 3 accompanists are allowed for each category."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["The theme of the item must not be cheap or vulgar.","A recorded tune is not allowed in the Ghazal and Geet categories."],"Judging":null,"Points":["Prizes for Ghazal and Geet are given separately at the Zonal and Inter-Zonal festivals."],"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Light Vocal has two categories: Ghazal and Geet, and Folk Song.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Each participant gets up to 6 minutes. Maximum 1 participant and 3 accompanists for each category.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- At the Zonal Festival each institution sends two participants: one from the Ghazal or Geet category and one from the Folk Song category.\\n- At the Inter-Zonal Festival each zone sends one participant from Ghazal (first position), one from Geet (first position) and two from Folk Song (first and second position).\\n- A student may not take part in more than one category.\\n- Harmonium is allowed.\\n- Up to 3 accompanists are allowed for each category.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- The theme of the item must not be cheap or vulgar.\\n- A recorded tune is not allowed in the Ghazal and Geet categories.\\n\\n## Points\\n- Prizes for Ghazal and Geet are given separately at the Zonal and Inter-Zonal festivals."},{"Title":"Shabad/Bhajan","Source":"Booklet 2026 p.23 Group Shabad & Group Bhajan, p.2 table","Sections":{"About":["This is a group item for Group Shabad and Group Bhajan."],"TimeAndFormat":["Time is up to 8 minutes."],"Rules":["At the Zonal Festival each institution sends only one team, for either Shabad or Bhajan.","At the Inter-Zonal Festival each zone sends one Shabad team (first position) and one Bhajan team (first position).","Up to 7 participants, not counting accompanists, are allowed at both the Zonal and Inter-Zonal festivals.","Up to 3 accompanists are allowed for each category.","In Shabad Gayan, a participant who chooses the Padtaal style must sing only the Bani of Guru Arjan Dev Ji or Guru Ramdas Ji under the title Padtaal."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":["Prizes for Group Shabad and Group Bhajan are given separately at the Zonal and Inter-Zonal festivals."],"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- This is a group item for Group Shabad and Group Bhajan.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Time is up to 8 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- At the Zonal Festival each institution sends only one team, for either Shabad or Bhajan.\\n- At the Inter-Zonal Festival each zone sends one Shabad team (first position) and one Bhajan team (first position).\\n- Up to 7 participants, not counting accompanists, are allowed at both the Zonal and Inter-Zonal festivals.\\n- Up to 3 accompanists are allowed for each category.\\n- In Shabad Gayan, a participant who chooses the Padtaal style must sing only the Bani of Guru Arjan Dev Ji or Guru Ramdas Ji under the title Padtaal.\\n\\n## Points\\n- Prizes for Group Shabad and Group Bhajan are given separately at the Zonal and Inter-Zonal festivals."},{"Title":"Group Singing (Indian)","Source":"Booklet 2026 p.23-24 Group Singing (Indian), p.2 table","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Maximum time is 10 minutes."],"Rules":["At the Zonal Festival each institution sends a team. At the Inter-Zonal Festival each zone sends two teams (first and second position).","A team may be all boys, all girls, or boys and girls together.","A team presents two songs: one patriotic and one folk song. Both songs are woven together and sung in one go.","A team has at most 6 singers. At most 3 accompanists play instruments.","The group song is taken from Indian songs. The folk song may be in a regional language (Punjabi)."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["No film song may be presented as the group song."],"Judging":["Judging is on the quality of singing only, not on make-up, costumes or actions of the teams."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Maximum time is 10 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- At the Zonal Festival each institution sends a team. At the Inter-Zonal Festival each zone sends two teams (first and second position).\\n- A team may be all boys, all girls, or boys and girls together.\\n- A team presents two songs: one patriotic and one folk song. Both songs are woven together and sung in one go.\\n- A team has at most 6 singers. At most 3 accompanists play instruments.\\n- The group song is taken from Indian songs. The folk song may be in a regional language (Punjabi).\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- No film song may be presented as the group song.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judging is on the quality of singing only, not on make-up, costumes or actions of the teams."},{"Title":"Classical Vocal","Source":"Booklet 2026 p.24 Classical Vocal, p.2 table","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Each participant gets up to 10 minutes."],"Rules":["At the Zonal Festival each institution sends one participant. At the Inter-Zonal Festival each zone sends two participants (first and second position).","Two styles are allowed: North Indian (Hindustani) and South Indian (Karnataka).","Two accompanists are allowed.","The harmonium may be used by the accompanist."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["The participant may not play the harmonium himself or herself."],"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Each participant gets up to 10 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- At the Zonal Festival each institution sends one participant. At the Inter-Zonal Festival each zone sends two participants (first and second position).\\n- Two styles are allowed: North Indian (Hindustani) and South Indian (Karnataka).\\n- Two accompanists are allowed.\\n- The harmonium may be used by the accompanist.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- The participant may not play the harmonium himself or herself."},{"Title":"Instrumental (Percussion)","Source":"Booklet 2026 p.24 Instrumental Music, p.2 table","Sections":{"About":["Category: Percussion (Taal Vadya)."],"TimeAndFormat":["Each participant gets up to 10 minutes."],"Rules":["At the Zonal Festival each institution sends one participant in this category. At the Inter-Zonal Festival each zone sends two participants (first and second position).","A student may not take part in more than one category (Percussion or Non-percussion).","Participants must bring their own instruments.","Two accompanists are allowed. The harmonium may be played by an accompanist."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["The harmonium is not allowed as the participant's instrument."],"Judging":null,"Points":["Awards are given category-wise."],"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Category: Percussion (Taal Vadya).\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Each participant gets up to 10 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- At the Zonal Festival each institution sends one participant in this category. At the Inter-Zonal Festival each zone sends two participants (first and second position).\\n- A student may not take part in more than one category (Percussion or Non-percussion).\\n- Participants must bring their own instruments.\\n- Two accompanists are allowed. The harmonium may be played by an accompanist.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- The harmonium is not allowed as the participant's instrument.\\n\\n## Points\\n- Awards are given category-wise."},{"Title":"Instrumental (Non-Percussion)","Source":"Booklet 2026 p.24 Instrumental Music, p.2 table","Sections":{"About":["Category: Non-percussion (Swar Vadya)."],"TimeAndFormat":["Each participant gets up to 10 minutes."],"Rules":["At the Zonal Festival each institution sends one participant in this category. At the Inter-Zonal Festival each zone sends two participants (first and second position).","A student may not take part in more than one category (Percussion or Non-percussion).","Participants must bring their own instruments.","Instruments of western origin adapted to the Indian Raga System, such as guitar and violin, are allowed.","Two accompanists are allowed. The harmonium may be played by an accompanist."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["The harmonium is not allowed as the participant's instrument."],"Judging":null,"Points":["Awards are given category-wise."],"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Category: Non-percussion (Swar Vadya).\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Each participant gets up to 10 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- At the Zonal Festival each institution sends one participant in this category. At the Inter-Zonal Festival each zone sends two participants (first and second position).\\n- A student may not take part in more than one category (Percussion or Non-percussion).\\n- Participants must bring their own instruments.\\n- Instruments of western origin adapted to the Indian Raga System, such as guitar and violin, are allowed.\\n- Two accompanists are allowed. The harmonium may be played by an accompanist.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- The harmonium is not allowed as the participant's instrument.\\n\\n## Points\\n- Awards are given category-wise."},{"Title":"Indian Orchestra","Source":"Booklet 2026 p.25 Indian Orchestra, p.2 table, p.13 rule 3","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Duration is up to 10 minutes.","Up to 10 minutes are given for stage-setting."],"Rules":["At the Zonal Festival each institution sends one team. At the Inter-Zonal Festival each zone sends two teams (first and second position).","A team has up to 8 participants.","Participants bring their own instruments.","At least five different instruments are included in the orchestra. Sitar and Madhuveena count as different instruments.","The director of the orchestra may take part as an accompanist.","An accompanist plays only one instrument. A student may play any number of instruments.","The total number of accompanists, including the director if on stage, is up to two."],"Allowed":["A tanpura is allowed to give the base."],"NotAllowed":["The tanpura is not allowed as an instrument of the orchestra."],"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Duration is up to 10 minutes.\\n- Up to 10 minutes are given for stage-setting.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- At the Zonal Festival each institution sends one team. At the Inter-Zonal Festival each zone sends two teams (first and second position).\\n- A team has up to 8 participants.\\n- Participants bring their own instruments.\\n- At least five different instruments are included in the orchestra. Sitar and Madhuveena count as different instruments.\\n- The director of the orchestra may take part as an accompanist.\\n- An accompanist plays only one instrument. A student may play any number of instruments.\\n- The total number of accompanists, including the director if on stage, is up to two.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- A tanpura is allowed to give the base.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- The tanpura is not allowed as an instrument of the orchestra."},{"Title":"Folk Orchestra","Source":"Booklet 2026 p.25 Folk Orchestra, p.2 table, p.13 rule 3","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Maximum duration is 10 minutes.","Up to 10 minutes are given for stage-setting."],"Rules":["At the Zonal Festival each institution sends one team. At the Inter-Zonal Festival each zone sends two teams (first and second position).","A team has up to 12 participants. It may be all boys, all girls, or combined.","Up to three professional accompanists are allowed. They wear a different dress from the student participants so that they are easy to identify.","The professional accompanists sit or stand separately from the participants and do not lead the team.","The team preferably presents folk tunes that are recognised as folk tunes of Punjab."],"Allowed":["Folk instruments allowed: Algozas, Been, Bansuri, Wanjhali, Sarangi, Dotara, King, Toombi, Toomba, Sankh, Dhol, Dholak (Dholaki), Duffli, Duff, Ghara, Bughchu, Dhad, Nagara, Hamel, Kato, Sapp, Dauru, Chimta, Khanjri, Manjeera, Dariya and Ghungroo."],"NotAllowed":["No other instrument or article is allowed."],"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Maximum duration is 10 minutes.\\n- Up to 10 minutes are given for stage-setting.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- At the Zonal Festival each institution sends one team. At the Inter-Zonal Festival each zone sends two teams (first and second position).\\n- A team has up to 12 participants. It may be all boys, all girls, or combined.\\n- Up to three professional accompanists are allowed. They wear a different dress from the student participants so that they are easy to identify.\\n- The professional accompanists sit or stand separately from the participants and do not lead the team.\\n- The team preferably presents folk tunes that are recognised as folk tunes of Punjab.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Folk instruments allowed: Algozas, Been, Bansuri, Wanjhali, Sarangi, Dotara, King, Toombi, Toomba, Sankh, Dhol, Dholak (Dholaki), Duffli, Duff, Ghara, Bughchu, Dhad, Nagara, Hamel, Kato, Sapp, Dauru, Chimta, Khanjri, Manjeera, Dariya and Ghungroo.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- No other instrument or article is allowed."},{"Title":"Classical Dance","Source":"Booklet 2026 p.27 Classical Dance, p.2 table","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["The performance lasts from 8 to 10 minutes."],"Rules":["At the Zonal Festival each institution sends one participant. At the Inter-Zonal Festival each zone sends two participants (first and second position).","The dance can be from any approved school of dance: Kathak, Kathakali, Bharatnatyam, Manipuri, Kuchipudi, Mohiniyattam, Odissi or Sattriya.","Three to five accompanists are allowed.","Accompaniment must be live."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Recorded music, audio or CDs are not permitted."],"Judging":["Judgment is based on Taal, technique, rhythm, abhinaya expression, costumes, footwork and overall impression."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- The performance lasts from 8 to 10 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- At the Zonal Festival each institution sends one participant. At the Inter-Zonal Festival each zone sends two participants (first and second position).\\n- The dance can be from any approved school of dance: Kathak, Kathakali, Bharatnatyam, Manipuri, Kuchipudi, Mohiniyattam, Odissi or Sattriya.\\n- Three to five accompanists are allowed.\\n- Accompaniment must be live.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Recorded music, audio or CDs are not permitted.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judgment is based on Taal, technique, rhythm, abhinaya expression, costumes, footwork and overall impression."},{"Title":"Giddha","Source":"Booklet 2026 p.27-28 Giddha, p.2 table","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Duration is up to 12 minutes.","Time is counted from the raising of the curtain. If there is no curtain, it is counted from the first beat of the dholak or the moment the participants start to perform (dance or sing), whichever is earlier."],"Rules":["At the Zonal Festival each institution sends one team. At the Inter-Zonal Festival each zone sends two teams (first and second position).","Actions follow the traditional dholak taals and the traditional style of boli singing. Giddha should be in rhythm. Unwanted chharappas (jumps) are not appreciated.","A team has 9 to 11 girl participants.","The dress follows Punjabi culture: Phulkari or dupatta, heavy ghaghras, heavy salvars, long shirts with full or three-fourth sleeves. A salvar under the ghaghra is allowed, but not a pajami. The paranda is fixed in the hair. Decoration on dress and make-up should not be too much.","Costumes and jewellery are close to the traditional dress of women. Minimum stage property is used, and only property that fits the boli.","The wording of the bolies is based on relations in Punjabi culture and on the theme.","The dance is performed in traditional style with authentic movements, natural rhythmic flow (not unnecessarily fast) and relevant traditional bolies, keeping the grace and majesty of the dance.","Only one accompanist, a dholak player, is allowed."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["The dance must not include ballet scenes.","Dhol is not permitted at all as an instrument of accompaniment.","Indecent or obscene bolies are not allowed. The team is penalised if they are used."],"Judging":null,"Points":["For a co-education institution that enters both Gidha and Bhangra, only the better score of the two counts in the overall score sheet."],"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Duration is up to 12 minutes.\\n- Time is counted from the raising of the curtain. If there is no curtain, it is counted from the first beat of the dholak or the moment the participants start to perform (dance or sing), whichever is earlier.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- At the Zonal Festival each institution sends one team. At the Inter-Zonal Festival each zone sends two teams (first and second position).\\n- Actions follow the traditional dholak taals and the traditional style of boli singing. Giddha should be in rhythm. Unwanted chharappas (jumps) are not appreciated.\\n- A team has 9 to 11 girl participants.\\n- The dress follows Punjabi culture: Phulkari or dupatta, heavy ghaghras, heavy salvars, long shirts with full or three-fourth sleeves. A salvar under the ghaghra is allowed, but not a pajami. The paranda is fixed in the hair. Decoration on dress and make-up should not be too much.\\n- Costumes and jewellery are close to the traditional dress of women. Minimum stage property is used, and only property that fits the boli.\\n- The wording of the bolies is based on relations in Punjabi culture and on the theme.\\n- The dance is performed in traditional style with authentic movements, natural rhythmic flow (not unnecessarily fast) and relevant traditional bolies, keeping the grace and majesty of the dance.\\n- Only one accompanist, a dholak player, is allowed.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- The dance must not include ballet scenes.\\n- Dhol is not permitted at all as an instrument of accompaniment.\\n- Indecent or obscene bolies are not allowed. The team is penalised if they are used.\\n\\n## Points\\n- For a co-education institution that enters both Gidha and Bhangra, only the better score of the two counts in the overall score sheet."},{"Title":"Bhangra","Source":"Booklet 2026 p.28-29 Bhangra, p.2 table","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Duration is up to 10 minutes.","Time is counted from the raising of the curtain, or from the first beat of the drum where there is no curtain."],"Rules":["At the Zonal Festival each institution sends one team. At the Inter-Zonal Festival each zone sends two teams (first and second position).","Actions follow the traditional forms of dhol rhythm such as bhangra, luddi, dhamal, mirza, fummniaan, sialkotiaa, dankra, chaala'n, laihria and pathania.","Bhangra starts with the beat of the dhol.","Along with other formations, Bhangra is also done in a circle. The entry is direct from behind the curtain or stage, and the exit from the stage is made while dancing.","A team has 8 boy participants.","Artists wear ghungrus on their feet. Neck ornaments are kaintha or taveet and ear ornaments are natiyan. The dress is a plain or printed chadra, white shirt with neck embroidery, jacket, turban, gota or embroidery on the patti, and a farla without gota that is part of the turban.","Up to 4 accompanists are allowed. One of them, the boli singer, must be a bona fide student. The accompanists dress differently from the student participants. They may play Dhol, Algoze, Toombi, Iktara, Chimta and Bughdu.","Both sides of the dhol are made of leather (chamra).","The boliaan are relevant to the male dancers and fit the taal as needed.","The dance is performed in traditional style with authentic movements, natural rhythmic flow (not unnecessarily fast) and relevant traditional bolies, keeping the grace and majesty of the dance.","Movement of the shoulders and flexibility should be visible. Participants may use fast action or creativity as needed."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["The dance must not include ballet scenes.","Commentary, vartak, song, couplet, enactment or any ceremony at the start is not allowed.","Individual performance of the dholi, bazigar and individual actions are not allowed.","Fummans are not allowed.","The dholi may not use the mike.","Indecent or obscene boli is not allowed. The boliaan must not be presented like a filmy chitarhaar."],"Judging":null,"Points":["For a co-education institution that enters both Gidha and Bhangra, only the better score of the two counts in the overall score sheet."],"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Duration is up to 10 minutes.\\n- Time is counted from the raising of the curtain, or from the first beat of the drum where there is no curtain.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- At the Zonal Festival each institution sends one team. At the Inter-Zonal Festival each zone sends two teams (first and second position).\\n- Actions follow the traditional forms of dhol rhythm such as bhangra, luddi, dhamal, mirza, fummniaan, sialkotiaa, dankra, chaala'n, laihria and pathania.\\n- Bhangra starts with the beat of the dhol.\\n- Along with other formations, Bhangra is also done in a circle. The entry is direct from behind the curtain or stage, and the exit from the stage is made while dancing.\\n- A team has 8 boy participants.\\n- Artists wear ghungrus on their feet. Neck ornaments are kaintha or taveet and ear ornaments are natiyan. The dress is a plain or printed chadra, white shirt with neck embroidery, jacket, turban, gota or embroidery on the patti, and a farla without gota that is part of the turban.\\n- Up to 4 accompanists are allowed. One of them, the boli singer, must be a bona fide student. The accompanists dress differently from the student participants. They may play Dhol, Algoze, Toombi, Iktara, Chimta and Bughdu.\\n- Both sides of the dhol are made of leather (chamra).\\n- The boliaan are relevant to the male dancers and fit the taal as needed.\\n- The dance is performed in traditional style with authentic movements, natural rhythmic flow (not unnecessarily fast) and relevant traditional bolies, keeping the grace and majesty of the dance.\\n- Movement of the shoulders and flexibility should be visible. Participants may use fast action or creativity as needed.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- The dance must not include ballet scenes.\\n- Commentary, vartak, song, couplet, enactment or any ceremony at the start is not allowed.\\n- Individual performance of the dholi, bazigar and individual actions are not allowed.\\n- Fummans are not allowed.\\n- The dholi may not use the mike.\\n- Indecent or obscene boli is not allowed. The boliaan must not be presented like a filmy chitarhaar.\\n\\n## Points\\n- For a co-education institution that enters both Gidha and Bhangra, only the better score of the two counts in the overall score sheet."},{"Title":"Group Dance (General)","Source":"Booklet 2026 p.29 Group Dance General, p.2 table","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Duration is up to 10 minutes."],"Rules":["At the Zonal Festival each institution sends one team. At the Inter-Zonal Festival each zone sends two teams (first and second position).","Any style from the Indian folk and tribal dance tradition is allowed, except Punjabi folk dances (Bhangra, Giddha, Jhummar, Sammi, Luddi, Dandaas and Malwai-Giddha).","A team has 6 to 10 participants.","A team may have boys, girls, or boys and girls together. A mixed team is allowed only if the dance form allows it.","Up to 5 accompanists are allowed."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Western group dance is not allowed.","The group dance must not include puppet dance.","The accompanying song must not have indecent or obscene wording."],"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Duration is up to 10 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- At the Zonal Festival each institution sends one team. At the Inter-Zonal Festival each zone sends two teams (first and second position).\\n- Any style from the Indian folk and tribal dance tradition is allowed, except Punjabi folk dances (Bhangra, Giddha, Jhummar, Sammi, Luddi, Dandaas and Malwai-Giddha).\\n- A team has 6 to 10 participants.\\n- A team may have boys, girls, or boys and girls together. A mixed team is allowed only if the dance form allows it.\\n- Up to 5 accompanists are allowed.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Western group dance is not allowed.\\n- The group dance must not include puppet dance.\\n- The accompanying song must not have indecent or obscene wording."},{"Title":"One Act Play","Source":"Booklet 2026 p.31 One Act Play, p.2 table, p.13 rule 3","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Duration is up to 30 minutes. Time is counted as soon as the curtain goes up or the introduction of the play starts, whichever is earlier.","Up to 10 minutes are given for stage-setting."],"Rules":["At the Zonal Festival each institution sends one team. At the Inter-Zonal Festival each zone sends two teams (first and second position).","The play may be in Hindi, Punjabi, Urdu or English.","It may be a one-act play or a portion of a larger play. The curtain, once lifted, is not dropped until the end of the play.","Three accompanists are allowed. An accompanist either speaks from the background or plays a musical instrument for background music.","Up to 9 participants are allowed.","Singing is allowed, but total singing time must not be more than 25 percent of the total time of the play.","No consideration is given to deviations from the original script. The spirit and theme of the original play must not be distorted when the play is adapted.","The same institution may not present a particular play for the next four years in Panjab University Youth Festivals.","A purely male or purely female cast gets no compensation. A boy may play the part of a girl and a girl the part of a boy.","Lighting and property such as ordinary furniture are supplied. The group arranges any special property.","The theme and its depiction must not hurt the personal or religious feelings of any person or community. It must suit the occasion and the taste of the general student audience. Plays alien to Indian traditions, culture and social life are not considered.","The college may be asked to give the permission letter from the writer of the play or story, if needed."],"Allowed":["Use of a tape-recorder or CD player is allowed."],"NotAllowed":["The play must not be an opera.","A play without dialogue (silent play) is not allowed."],"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Duration is up to 30 minutes. Time is counted as soon as the curtain goes up or the introduction of the play starts, whichever is earlier.\\n- Up to 10 minutes are given for stage-setting.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- At the Zonal Festival each institution sends one team. At the Inter-Zonal Festival each zone sends two teams (first and second position).\\n- The play may be in Hindi, Punjabi, Urdu or English.\\n- It may be a one-act play or a portion of a larger play. The curtain, once lifted, is not dropped until the end of the play.\\n- Three accompanists are allowed. An accompanist either speaks from the background or plays a musical instrument for background music.\\n- Up to 9 participants are allowed.\\n- Singing is allowed, but total singing time must not be more than 25 percent of the total time of the play.\\n- No consideration is given to deviations from the original script. The spirit and theme of the original play must not be distorted when the play is adapted.\\n- The same institution may not present a particular play for the next four years in Panjab University Youth Festivals.\\n- A purely male or purely female cast gets no compensation. A boy may play the part of a girl and a girl the part of a boy.\\n- Lighting and property such as ordinary furniture are supplied. The group arranges any special property.\\n- The theme and its depiction must not hurt the personal or religious feelings of any person or community. It must suit the occasion and the taste of the general student audience. Plays alien to Indian traditions, culture and social life are not considered.\\n- The college may be asked to give the permission letter from the writer of the play or story, if needed.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Use of a tape-recorder or CD player is allowed.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- The play must not be an opera.\\n- A play without dialogue (silent play) is not allowed."},{"Title":"Skit","Source":"Booklet 2026 p.32 Skit, p.2 table","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Maximum time is 10 minutes."],"Rules":["At the Zonal Festival each institution sends one team. At the Inter-Zonal Festival each zone sends two teams (first and second position).","A team can have six participants.","Two accompanists are allowed. An accompanist either speaks from the background or plays a musical instrument for background music."],"Allowed":["Make-up, drapery and background music are allowed. Recorded background music is allowed."],"NotAllowed":["The theme and its depiction must not be obscene, vulgar, or hurtful to the personal or religious feelings of any person or community."],"Judging":["Judgement is based on theme, acting, stagecraft, design and overall impression."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Maximum time is 10 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- At the Zonal Festival each institution sends one team. At the Inter-Zonal Festival each zone sends two teams (first and second position).\\n- A team can have six participants.\\n- Two accompanists are allowed. An accompanist either speaks from the background or plays a musical instrument for background music.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Make-up, drapery and background music are allowed. Recorded background music is allowed.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- The theme and its depiction must not be obscene, vulgar, or hurtful to the personal or religious feelings of any person or community.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judgement is based on theme, acting, stagecraft, design and overall impression."},{"Title":"Mime","Source":"Booklet 2026 p.32 Mime, p.2 table","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Time is up to 5 minutes."],"Rules":["At the Zonal Festival each institution sends one team. At the Inter-Zonal Festival each zone sends two teams (first and second position).","Up to six participants are allowed in a team.","Two accompanists are allowed."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Judgement is based on idea, creativity of presentation, use of make-up, music and overall impression."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Time is up to 5 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- At the Zonal Festival each institution sends one team. At the Inter-Zonal Festival each zone sends two teams (first and second position).\\n- Up to six participants are allowed in a team.\\n- Two accompanists are allowed.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judgement is based on idea, creativity of presentation, use of make-up, music and overall impression."},{"Title":"Mimicry","Source":"Booklet 2026 p.32 Mimicry, p.2 table","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Each participant gets up to 5 minutes."],"Rules":["At the Zonal Festival each institution sends one participant. At the Inter-Zonal Festival each zone sends two participants (first and second position)."],"Allowed":["Participants may mimic the speech mannerisms of prominent persons including film actors and actresses, and sounds of machines, birds and musical instruments."],"NotAllowed":["The theme and its presentation must not be cheap, vulgar, or hurtful to the personal or religious feelings of any person or community."],"Judging":["Judgement is based on skill in imitating, variety of sounds and voices imitated, and presentation."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Each participant gets up to 5 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- At the Zonal Festival each institution sends one participant. At the Inter-Zonal Festival each zone sends two participants (first and second position).\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Participants may mimic the speech mannerisms of prominent persons including film actors and actresses, and sounds of machines, birds and musical instruments.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- The theme and its presentation must not be cheap, vulgar, or hurtful to the personal or religious feelings of any person or community.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judgement is based on skill in imitating, variety of sounds and voices imitated, and presentation."},{"Title":"Histrionics","Source":"Booklet 2026 p.33 Histrionics, p.2 table","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["A participant gets up to 6 minutes to show his or her talent.","Time is counted as soon as the participant starts the introduction, or starts the performance if there is no introduction."],"Rules":["At the Zonal Festival each institution sends one participant. At the Inter-Zonal Festival each zone sends two participants (first and second position).","A participant must show at least two characters."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["The theme and its presentation must not be cheap, vulgar, or hurtful to the personal or religious feelings of any person or community.","Mime is not allowed.","Extra equipment such as a stick, spectacles, book or chair is not allowed."],"Judging":["Dress and make-up are not considered in the judgement."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- A participant gets up to 6 minutes to show his or her talent.\\n- Time is counted as soon as the participant starts the introduction, or starts the performance if there is no introduction.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- At the Zonal Festival each institution sends one participant. At the Inter-Zonal Festival each zone sends two participants (first and second position).\\n- A participant must show at least two characters.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- The theme and its presentation must not be cheap, vulgar, or hurtful to the personal or religious feelings of any person or community.\\n- Mime is not allowed.\\n- Extra equipment such as a stick, spectacles, book or chair is not allowed.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Dress and make-up are not considered in the judgement."},{"Title":"Poem Recitation","Source":"Booklet 2026 p.35 Poem Recitation, p.2 table","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Maximum time for each participant is 5 minutes."],"Rules":["At the Zonal Festival each institution sends one participant. At the Inter-Zonal Festival each zone sends two participants (first and second position).","The poem may be recited in Punjabi, Hindi, English or Urdu.","The poem may be by any writer, or self-composed.","The participant says the name of the writer or the book from which the poem is taken."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Maximum time for each participant is 5 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- At the Zonal Festival each institution sends one participant. At the Inter-Zonal Festival each zone sends two participants (first and second position).\\n- The poem may be recited in Punjabi, Hindi, English or Urdu.\\n- The poem may be by any writer, or self-composed.\\n- The participant says the name of the writer or the book from which the poem is taken."},{"Title":"Debate","Source":"Booklet 2026 p.35 Debate, p.2 table, p.20 rule 20","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Each participant gets up to 5 minutes to speak."],"Rules":["At the Zonal Festival each institution sends two participants. At the Inter-Zonal Festival each zone sends two participants (first and second position).","A participant may speak in Punjabi, Hindi, English or Urdu.","The subject for the debate is announced 24 hours before the programme.","Lots are drawn 24 hours before the programme to decide whether a participant speaks for or against the motion.","The first speaker is invited again to speak for two minutes immediately after the last participant has finished. This second speech is not given any weight in the judgment. No other speaker gets a second chance.","On the conclusion of the debate, the Chairperson (Sabhapati) appointed by the Director Youth Welfare puts the motion before the general house for approval."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["No questions are allowed during or after a debate."],"Judging":["Judgement is based on individual performance."],"Points":["Debate is counted as an individual item for the overall trophy score."],"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Each participant gets up to 5 minutes to speak.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- At the Zonal Festival each institution sends two participants. At the Inter-Zonal Festival each zone sends two participants (first and second position).\\n- A participant may speak in Punjabi, Hindi, English or Urdu.\\n- The subject for the debate is announced 24 hours before the programme.\\n- Lots are drawn 24 hours before the programme to decide whether a participant speaks for or against the motion.\\n- The first speaker is invited again to speak for two minutes immediately after the last participant has finished. This second speech is not given any weight in the judgment. No other speaker gets a second chance.\\n- On the conclusion of the debate, the Chairperson (Sabhapati) appointed by the Director Youth Welfare puts the motion before the general house for approval.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- No questions are allowed during or after a debate.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judgement is based on individual performance.\\n\\n## Points\\n- Debate is counted as an individual item for the overall trophy score."},{"Title":"Elocution","Source":"Booklet 2026 p.36 Elocution, p.2 table","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Each speaker may speak for a maximum of 5 minutes."],"Rules":["At the Zonal Festival each institution sends one participant. At the Inter-Zonal Festival each zone sends two participants (first and second position).","The medium of expression is Punjabi, Hindi, English or Urdu.","The subject or topic is announced 24 hours before the programme."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Each speaker may speak for a maximum of 5 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- At the Zonal Festival each institution sends one participant. At the Inter-Zonal Festival each zone sends two participants (first and second position).\\n- The medium of expression is Punjabi, Hindi, English or Urdu.\\n- The subject or topic is announced 24 hours before the programme."},{"Title":"Quiz","Source":"Booklet 2026 p.36-37 Quiz, p.2 table","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["At the Zonal Festival each institution sends a team of three participants. At the Inter-Zonal Festival each zone sends two teams of six participants (first and second position).","There is a written preliminary round where each team answers questions together.","The questions, in the preliminary round and the finals, may be a mix of text-based and audio-visual questions.","The top six teams go to the finals, depending on the number of participating teams and the quiz master's discretion.","Once a team is in the final round, its preliminary score is not given any weight.","Teams are given their seating order in the finals at random, to remove bias.","The finals have different rounds with audio-visual questions. Unanswered questions are passed clockwise or anti-clockwise.","The first answer clearly heard by the Quiz Master from a team is final.","The quiz has questions of national and international importance on many topics, including: General Awareness (science, technology, history, polity, geography, business and economics); Arts and Culture (music, entertainment, literature, arts and pop culture); Sports and Recreation (sports, games, tournaments and sporting legends); and Current Affairs (recent happenings around the globe).","The scoring and evaluation procedure, the time to answer a question and the type of rounds are given before the competition starts.","In a tie, the Quiz Master may ask tie-breaker questions to decide the winners.","The decision of the Quiz Master is final and binding."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Unfair means, electronic devices and outside help are strictly prohibited. A team that breaks this rule is disqualified at once."],"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":["The booklet prints no time limit for the Quiz."]},"Markdown":"## Rules\\n- At the Zonal Festival each institution sends a team of three participants. At the Inter-Zonal Festival each zone sends two teams of six participants (first and second position).\\n- There is a written preliminary round where each team answers questions together.\\n- The questions, in the preliminary round and the finals, may be a mix of text-based and audio-visual questions.\\n- The top six teams go to the finals, depending on the number of participating teams and the quiz master's discretion.\\n- Once a team is in the final round, its preliminary score is not given any weight.\\n- Teams are given their seating order in the finals at random, to remove bias.\\n- The finals have different rounds with audio-visual questions. Unanswered questions are passed clockwise or anti-clockwise.\\n- The first answer clearly heard by the Quiz Master from a team is final.\\n- The quiz has questions of national and international importance on many topics, including: General Awareness (science, technology, history, polity, geography, business and economics); Arts and Culture (music, entertainment, literature, arts and pop culture); Sports and Recreation (sports, games, tournaments and sporting legends); and Current Affairs (recent happenings around the globe).\\n- The scoring and evaluation procedure, the time to answer a question and the type of rounds are given before the competition starts.\\n- In a tie, the Quiz Master may ask tie-breaker questions to decide the winners.\\n- The decision of the Quiz Master is final and binding.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Unfair means, electronic devices and outside help are strictly prohibited. A team that breaks this rule is disqualified at once.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- The booklet prints no time limit for the Quiz."},{"Title":"Creative Writing (Poem/Story/Essay)","Source":"Booklet 2026 p.37 Creative Writing, p.2 table","Sections":{"About":["Creative Writing has three categories: Poem Writing, Short-Story Writing and Essay Writing."],"TimeAndFormat":["Two hours are given for the competition in each category."],"Rules":["At the Zonal Festival each institution sends one participant for each category.","At the Inter-Zonal Festival each zone sends two participants (first and second position) in Poem Writing, two in Short-Story Writing and two in Essay Writing.","One student can take part in one category only.","The themes are announced on the spot.","The language is Punjabi, Hindi, Urdu or English."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["The depiction of the theme must not hurt the personal or religious feelings of any person or community."],"Judging":null,"Points":["Prizes for Poem, Short Story and Essay Writing are given separately at the Zonal and Inter-Zonal festivals."],"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Creative Writing has three categories: Poem Writing, Short-Story Writing and Essay Writing.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Two hours are given for the competition in each category.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- At the Zonal Festival each institution sends one participant for each category.\\n- At the Inter-Zonal Festival each zone sends two participants (first and second position) in Poem Writing, two in Short-Story Writing and two in Essay Writing.\\n- One student can take part in one category only.\\n- The themes are announced on the spot.\\n- The language is Punjabi, Hindi, Urdu or English.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- The depiction of the theme must not hurt the personal or religious feelings of any person or community.\\n\\n## Points\\n- Prizes for Poem, Short Story and Essay Writing are given separately at the Zonal and Inter-Zonal festivals."},{"Title":"On-the-Spot Painting","Source":"Booklet 2026 p.40-41 On the Spot Painting, p.2 table","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Time to finish the painting is 2 hours 30 minutes."],"Rules":["At the Zonal Festival each institution sends two participants. At the Inter-Zonal Festival each zone sends three participants (first, second and third position).","One student can take part in only one category of Group A (On the Spot Painting, Photography, Collage Making, Clay Modelling, Rangoli). If Rangoli is held on another day, a student who took part in a Group A category may also be allowed to take part in Rangoli.","The participant may use any of these media: oil paint, water colours, pencils, ink, poster colours or pastel colours.","The size of the sheet or board is a half imperial sheet, 22 x 15 inches (50 x 35 cm).","Participants prepare compositions on an actual location, a theme or an imaginary situation given on the spot.","The host college gives good quality paper or sheet as needed."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Time to finish the painting is 2 hours 30 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- At the Zonal Festival each institution sends two participants. At the Inter-Zonal Festival each zone sends three participants (first, second and third position).\\n- One student can take part in only one category of Group A (On the Spot Painting, Photography, Collage Making, Clay Modelling, Rangoli). If Rangoli is held on another day, a student who took part in a Group A category may also be allowed to take part in Rangoli.\\n- The participant may use any of these media: oil paint, water colours, pencils, ink, poster colours or pastel colours.\\n- The size of the sheet or board is a half imperial sheet, 22 x 15 inches (50 x 35 cm).\\n- Participants prepare compositions on an actual location, a theme or an imaginary situation given on the spot.\\n- The host college gives good quality paper or sheet as needed."},{"Title":"Photography","Source":"Booklet 2026 p.41 Photography, p.2 table","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["The time limit is 2 hours 30 minutes."],"Rules":["At the Zonal Festival each institution sends two participants. At the Inter-Zonal Festival each zone sends three participants (first, second and third position).","One student can take part in only one category of Group A (On the Spot Painting, Photography, Collage Making, Clay Modelling, Rangoli). If Rangoli is held on another day, a student who took part in a Group A category may also be allowed to take part in Rangoli.","The participant brings his or her own digital camera.","The digital camera must have a memory card. The judges format it before the contest starts.","The participant takes 5 photographs on the theme announced on the spot by the judges.","The organisers have all rights to use the pictures as they see fit.","Extra instructions, if any, are announced on the spot."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["A mobile phone is not allowed for Photography.","No mixing, matching or morphing of photographs is permitted.","Software such as Photoshop to enhance images is not permitted."],"Judging":["Digital images are judged on impact, composition, technical quality and suitability for the theme."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- The time limit is 2 hours 30 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- At the Zonal Festival each institution sends two participants. At the Inter-Zonal Festival each zone sends three participants (first, second and third position).\\n- One student can take part in only one category of Group A (On the Spot Painting, Photography, Collage Making, Clay Modelling, Rangoli). If Rangoli is held on another day, a student who took part in a Group A category may also be allowed to take part in Rangoli.\\n- The participant brings his or her own digital camera.\\n- The digital camera must have a memory card. The judges format it before the contest starts.\\n- The participant takes 5 photographs on the theme announced on the spot by the judges.\\n- The organisers have all rights to use the pictures as they see fit.\\n- Extra instructions, if any, are announced on the spot.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- A mobile phone is not allowed for Photography.\\n- No mixing, matching or morphing of photographs is permitted.\\n- Software such as Photoshop to enhance images is not permitted.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Digital images are judged on impact, composition, technical quality and suitability for the theme."},{"Title":"Collage Making","Source":"Booklet 2026 p.42 Collage Making, p.2 table","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Duration is not more than 2 hours 30 minutes."],"Rules":["At the Zonal Festival each institution sends two participants. At the Inter-Zonal Festival each zone sends three participants (first, second and third position).","One student can take part in only one category of Group A (On the Spot Painting, Photography, Collage Making, Clay Modelling, Rangoli). If Rangoli is held on another day, a student who took part in a Group A category may also be allowed to take part in Rangoli.","The item is conducted on the spot.","Participants bring their own scissors and other material.","The collage is made from old magazines. The host college gives drawing paper of size 22 x 15 inches."],"Allowed":["Cutting material with an instrument is allowed. Tearing material into pieces is appreciated.","Waste material is allowed.","Any type of base is allowed.","A pencil may be used to draw objects or figures on the base or sheet."],"NotAllowed":["A marker, pen or paint brush may not be used for writing or calligraphic work on the collage."],"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Duration is not more than 2 hours 30 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- At the Zonal Festival each institution sends two participants. At the Inter-Zonal Festival each zone sends three participants (first, second and third position).\\n- One student can take part in only one category of Group A (On the Spot Painting, Photography, Collage Making, Clay Modelling, Rangoli). If Rangoli is held on another day, a student who took part in a Group A category may also be allowed to take part in Rangoli.\\n- The item is conducted on the spot.\\n- Participants bring their own scissors and other material.\\n- The collage is made from old magazines. The host college gives drawing paper of size 22 x 15 inches.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Cutting material with an instrument is allowed. Tearing material into pieces is appreciated.\\n- Waste material is allowed.\\n- Any type of base is allowed.\\n- A pencil may be used to draw objects or figures on the base or sheet.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- A marker, pen or paint brush may not be used for writing or calligraphic work on the collage."},{"Title":"Clay Modelling","Source":"Booklet 2026 p.42 Clay-Modelling, p.2 table","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Time allowed is not more than 2 hours 30 minutes."],"Rules":["At the Zonal Festival each institution sends two participants. At the Inter-Zonal Festival each zone sends three participants (first, second and third position).","One student can take part in only one category of Group A (On the Spot Painting, Photography, Collage Making, Clay Modelling, Rangoli). If Rangoli is held on another day, a student who took part in a Group A category may also be allowed to take part in Rangoli.","The item is conducted on the spot.","The minimum height of the model is 10 inches.","Artificial clay is allowed. Natural clay is appreciated.","The host college does not provide clay. Participants bring their own clay."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Time allowed is not more than 2 hours 30 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- At the Zonal Festival each institution sends two participants. At the Inter-Zonal Festival each zone sends three participants (first, second and third position).\\n- One student can take part in only one category of Group A (On the Spot Painting, Photography, Collage Making, Clay Modelling, Rangoli). If Rangoli is held on another day, a student who took part in a Group A category may also be allowed to take part in Rangoli.\\n- The item is conducted on the spot.\\n- The minimum height of the model is 10 inches.\\n- Artificial clay is allowed. Natural clay is appreciated.\\n- The host college does not provide clay. Participants bring their own clay."},{"Title":"Cartooning","Source":"Booklet 2026 p.42 Cartooning, p.2 table","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Time allowed is not more than 2 hours 30 minutes."],"Rules":["At the Zonal Festival each institution sends two participants. At the Inter-Zonal Festival each zone sends three participants (first, second and third position).","One student can take part in only one category of Group B (Cartooning, Still Life Drawing, Poster Making, Installation).","The item is conducted on the spot on a given subject or idea.","Participants bring their own material. The host college gives only drawing paper of 22 x 15 inches."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Time allowed is not more than 2 hours 30 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- At the Zonal Festival each institution sends two participants. At the Inter-Zonal Festival each zone sends three participants (first, second and third position).\\n- One student can take part in only one category of Group B (Cartooning, Still Life Drawing, Poster Making, Installation).\\n- The item is conducted on the spot on a given subject or idea.\\n- Participants bring their own material. The host college gives only drawing paper of 22 x 15 inches."},{"Title":"Still Life Drawing","Source":"Booklet 2026 p.43 Still Life Drawing, p.2 table","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Time to finish the painting is 2 hours 30 minutes."],"Rules":["At the Zonal Festival each institution sends two participants. At the Inter-Zonal Festival each zone sends three participants (first, second and third position).","One student can take part in only one category of Group B (Cartooning, Still Life Drawing, Poster Making, Installation).","The participant may use any of these media: oil paint, water colours, pencils, ink, poster colours or pastel colours.","The size of the sheet or board is a half imperial sheet, 22 x 15 inches (50 x 35 cm).","Participants bring their own material for painting.","The judges or the host college set up the still life scene.","The host college gives good quality paper or sheet as needed."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Time to finish the painting is 2 hours 30 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- At the Zonal Festival each institution sends two participants. At the Inter-Zonal Festival each zone sends three participants (first, second and third position).\\n- One student can take part in only one category of Group B (Cartooning, Still Life Drawing, Poster Making, Installation).\\n- The participant may use any of these media: oil paint, water colours, pencils, ink, poster colours or pastel colours.\\n- The size of the sheet or board is a half imperial sheet, 22 x 15 inches (50 x 35 cm).\\n- Participants bring their own material for painting.\\n- The judges or the host college set up the still life scene.\\n- The host college gives good quality paper or sheet as needed."},{"Title":"Rangoli","Source":"Booklet 2026 p.40 note, p.43 Rangoli, p.2 table","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Time allowed is 2 hours 30 minutes."],"Rules":["At the Zonal Festival each institution sends two participants. At the Inter-Zonal Festival each zone sends three participants (first, second and third position).","One student can take part in only one category of Group A (On the Spot Painting, Photography, Collage Making, Clay Modelling, Rangoli). If Rangoli is held on another day, a student who took part in a Group A category may also be allowed to take part in Rangoli.","The item is conducted on the spot on a given subject or idea.","Each rangoli design may be at most 4 feet x 4 feet (4 feet across for a circular rangoli) and not smaller than 2.5 feet x 2.5 feet (2.5 feet across for a circular rangoli). It must be made within and on the space given by the organisers.","Only dry material is allowed for colours.","Only traditional themes are given. Creativity in the overall pattern is appreciated.","Participants bring their own material, such as pulses, cereals, dry powder, saw-dust, flowers and green leaves.","This art is called by different names in different regions, such as Mandna, Alpana, Alekhan, Kolam and Rangoli. The medium and form of expression may be free hand, pictorial and descriptive.","To draw the design, participants may use chalk, pencil, marker and scale."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Stencils are prohibited."],"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Time allowed is 2 hours 30 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- At the Zonal Festival each institution sends two participants. At the Inter-Zonal Festival each zone sends three participants (first, second and third position).\\n- One student can take part in only one category of Group A (On the Spot Painting, Photography, Collage Making, Clay Modelling, Rangoli). If Rangoli is held on another day, a student who took part in a Group A category may also be allowed to take part in Rangoli.\\n- The item is conducted on the spot on a given subject or idea.\\n- Each rangoli design may be at most 4 feet x 4 feet (4 feet across for a circular rangoli) and not smaller than 2.5 feet x 2.5 feet (2.5 feet across for a circular rangoli). It must be made within and on the space given by the organisers.\\n- Only dry material is allowed for colours.\\n- Only traditional themes are given. Creativity in the overall pattern is appreciated.\\n- Participants bring their own material, such as pulses, cereals, dry powder, saw-dust, flowers and green leaves.\\n- This art is called by different names in different regions, such as Mandna, Alpana, Alekhan, Kolam and Rangoli. The medium and form of expression may be free hand, pictorial and descriptive.\\n- To draw the design, participants may use chalk, pencil, marker and scale.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Stencils are prohibited."},{"Title":"Poster Making","Source":"Booklet 2026 p.43-44 Poster-Making, p.2 table","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Time allowed is not more than 2 hours 30 minutes."],"Rules":["At the Zonal Festival each institution sends two participants. At the Inter-Zonal Festival each zone sends three participants (first, second and third position).","One student can take part in only one category of Group B (Cartooning, Still Life Drawing, Poster Making, Installation).","The item is conducted on the spot, and participants make a poster on a given subject.","Pasting extra material is not appreciated.","Participants bring their own material such as sheets, brushes and colours. The host college gives only drawing paper or sheet of 22 x 15 inches."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Time allowed is not more than 2 hours 30 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- At the Zonal Festival each institution sends two participants. At the Inter-Zonal Festival each zone sends three participants (first, second and third position).\\n- One student can take part in only one category of Group B (Cartooning, Still Life Drawing, Poster Making, Installation).\\n- The item is conducted on the spot, and participants make a poster on a given subject.\\n- Pasting extra material is not appreciated.\\n- Participants bring their own material such as sheets, brushes and colours. The host college gives only drawing paper or sheet of 22 x 15 inches."},{"Title":"Installation","Source":"Booklet 2026 p.44 Installation, p.2 table","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Time allowed is 2 hours 30 minutes. The theme is announced two hours before the competition starts."],"Rules":["At the Zonal Festival each institution sends one team of four students. At the Inter-Zonal Festival each zone sends two teams (first and second position).","One student can take part in only one category of Group B (Cartooning, Still Life Drawing, Poster Making, Installation).","The host college appoints a supervisor, with the approval of the Director Youth Welfare, to check the raw material of the teams before and during the competition.","Participants may use all the material they use in other art items such as cartooning, painting, rangoli, poster, collage and clay modelling to install or create an atmosphere related to the subject or title of the installation.","Participants may use waste material available around them, or take any material from outside.","This is a group activity. Four participants take part, but they make only one installation. Its size must not be bigger than 5 x 5 x 5 inches."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Participants may not use already composed images or forms available in the market. They must make their own image from the raw material."],"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Time allowed is 2 hours 30 minutes. The theme is announced two hours before the competition starts.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- At the Zonal Festival each institution sends one team of four students. At the Inter-Zonal Festival each zone sends two teams (first and second position).\\n- One student can take part in only one category of Group B (Cartooning, Still Life Drawing, Poster Making, Installation).\\n- The host college appoints a supervisor, with the approval of the Director Youth Welfare, to check the raw material of the teams before and during the competition.\\n- Participants may use all the material they use in other art items such as cartooning, painting, rangoli, poster, collage and clay modelling to install or create an atmosphere related to the subject or title of the installation.\\n- Participants may use waste material available around them, or take any material from outside.\\n- This is a group activity. Four participants take part, but they make only one installation. Its size must not be bigger than 5 x 5 x 5 inches.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Participants may not use already composed images or forms available in the market. They must make their own image from the raw material."}]`),s=[],r=[{Key:"ZonalFestivalDates",Kind:"date",Label:"Zonal Youth and Heritage Festival dates",Value:"To be announced by the Department of Youth Welfare",Source:"Booklet 2026 p.7 (venue and dates will be notified by the Department of Youth Welfare)"},{Key:"ZonalFestivalVenue",Kind:"address",Label:"Zonal Youth Festival venue (host college of each zone)",Value:{Name:"To be announced (host college of the zone)",Address:"",City:"",MapUrl:"",Directions:""},Source:"Booklet 2026 p.7 and p.13 (any institution may host the festival of its zone; the venue is notified)"},{Key:"InterZonalFestivalDates",Kind:"date",Label:"Inter-Zonal Youth and Heritage Festival dates",Value:"To be announced by the Department of Youth Welfare",Source:"Booklet 2026 p.13 rule 5(c) (dates and venue decided by the Department and notified well in time)"},{Key:"InterZonalFestivalVenue",Kind:"address",Label:"Inter-Zonal Youth Festival venue",Value:{Name:"To be announced (decided by the Department of Youth Welfare)",Address:"",City:"",MapUrl:"",Directions:""},Source:"Booklet 2026 p.13 rule 5(c)"},{Key:"AgeLimit",Kind:"text",Label:"Age limit",Value:"Under 25 years on the first day of July of the relevant session",Source:"Booklet 2026 p.12 rule 2(a)"},{Key:"ZonalYouthEntryFee",Kind:"fee",Label:"Zonal Youth Festival entry fee",Value:"Rs. 11 per student on the rolls of the institution",Source:"Booklet 2026 p.11 rule 1 Subsidy & Entry Fee"},{Key:"ZonalHeritageEntryFee",Kind:"fee",Label:"Zonal Heritage Festival entry fee",Value:"Rs. 6 per student on the rolls of the institution",Source:"Booklet 2026 p.11 rule 1"},{Key:"HostContribution",Kind:"fee",Label:"Youth festival contribution to the host college (Zonal Festival)",Value:"Rs. 12,000 for a college with up to 500 students; Rs. 15,000 for a college with more than 500 students; Rs. 20,000 for an education college (whatever its strength)",Source:"Booklet 2026 p.11 rule 1"},{Key:"ObjectionFee",Kind:"fee",Label:"Fee to lodge an objection or complaint",Value:"Rs. 2,000 in cash",Source:"Booklet 2026 p.18 rule 17(c)"},{Key:"UniversitySubsidy",Kind:"fee",Label:"University subsidy for each festival (from the Youth Welfare Fund Account)",Value:"Inter-Zonal Youth Festival Rs. 12,00,000; Inter-Zonal Heritage Festival Rs. 6,00,000; Zonal Youth Festival Rs. 4,00,000; Zonal Heritage Festival Rs. 2,00,000",Source:"Booklet 2026 p.11 rule 1"},{Key:"JudgesPayment",Kind:"fee",Label:"Payments to judges and the Quiz Master",Value:"Outstation judges: Rs. 15 per km as T.A. with D.A. as per university rules. Local judges: local conveyance as per university rules. Honorarium Rs. 1,000 per session, and a maximum of Rs. 1,500 if the session continues beyond 7 hours. Quiz Master: Rs. 1,500 per day with T.A./D.A. as per university rules.",Source:"Booklet 2026 p.15-16 rule 13(b)"},{Key:"DepartmentContact",Kind:"contact",Label:"Contact: Department of Youth Welfare",Value:{Name:"Dr. Sukhjinder Rishi",Role:"Director Youth Welfare, Panjab University, Chandigarh",Phone:"0172-2784448, 0172-2534152, 0172-2534153",WhatsApp:"",Email:"youthwelfare@pu.ac.in, dywpu14@gmail.com"},Source:"Booklet 2026 inside cover (Issued by) and back page (Published by: Dr. Sukhjinder Rishi, Director Youth Welfare)"},{Key:"DepartmentAddress",Kind:"address",Label:"Office of the Department of Youth Welfare",Value:{Name:"Department of Youth Welfare, Panjab University",Address:"",City:"Chandigarh",MapUrl:"",Directions:""},Source:"Booklet 2026 cover and entry forms (Department of Youth Welfare, Panjab University, Chandigarh; no street address printed)"}],l=[{Claim:"Levels, items, eligibility, entry limits, time limits, prizes, overall trophies, complaints and entry forms for the Panjab University Youth Festival, September 2026 edition.",SourceType:"Primary - organiser's own rules booklet",Source:"Panjab University Youth & Heritage Festivals - Information and Rules Booklet, September 2026",Url:"https://youthwelfare.puchd.ac.in/pu-yw-information-and-rules-booklet-2026.pdf"},{Claim:"Department contact numbers and email addresses (issued by Director Youth Welfare).",SourceType:"Primary - organiser's own rules booklet",Source:"Booklet 2026 inside cover",Url:"https://youthwelfare.puchd.ac.in/pu-yw-information-and-rules-booklet-2026.pdf"}],d={TemplateKey:e,Year:2026,Note:t,Page:a,ParticipantTypes:n,AgeGroups:o,Competitions:i,CompetitionAgeGroups:s,Variables:r,Evidence:l};export{o as AgeGroups,s as CompetitionAgeGroups,i as Competitions,l as Evidence,t as Note,a as Page,n as ParticipantTypes,e as TemplateKey,r as Variables,h as Year,d as default};
